WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.280
Let’s talk about that explosion.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.680
It was late afternoon in Beirut.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.280
People were watching a huge fire take hold in the port.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.120
But no one expected this.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.600
Two days after the disaster

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.760
more than 135 people have died.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.280
We may never know the real number.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.920
Ambulances continue to arrive at the scene of the explosion.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.520
Thousands were injured.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.640
Beirut's governor says more than 300,000 people are now homeless.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.600
So what do we know about why this happened?

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.560
What is it about Lebanon that makes this so much worse?

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.560
And how will a country that's almost bankrupt ever rebuild?

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.080
Lebanon was already on its knees.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.400
Debt, poverty, conflict, a paralysed government

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:51.880
corruption, money that's almost worthless. And then this.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.640
"Everyone has a story of survival and tragedy."

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.440
It's hard to make sense of the devastation.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.560
But this is what the port area used to look like.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.880
It's surrounded by people's homes.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.160
And that's the warehouse by the water where nearly

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.200
3,000 tonnes of ammonium nitrate were being stored.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.960
The chemical is a common fertilizer and you can use it to make explosives.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:30.320
That's what a bomber did in Oklahoma City in 1995.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.960
The fertilizer arrived at the port on a vessel

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.000
that was having technical problems.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.440
It was then reportedly impounded.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.880
Over the years, requests to do something about it

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.320
either by selling it locally or exporting it

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.560
were apparently sent to the courts.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.800
But nothing happened.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.720
And now they're trying to figure out who's responsible for the explosion.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.800
The president of Lebanon says an investigation into the Beirut port explosion 

00:02:53.800 --> 00:03:00.240
will look at whether it was caused by negligence, an accident, or possible external interference.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.400
People in Lebanon also want answers.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.400
People are in shock but anger is also growing at a political class

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.160
many blame for mismanagement and being responsible for running the economy into the ground.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.840
It's an economic crisis made much worse by a pandemic and lockdowns.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.480
But they were protesting long before COVID-19.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.400
To understand what's behind Lebanon's economic and political crisis

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.200
here's part of our explainer from back in February.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.560
Protesters say they're fed up with a lot of things:

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:59.640
the economy, high taxes, lack of jobs, crumbling infrastructure

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.800
and they say the biggest problem is rampant corruption whoch has thrived

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.920
under Lebanon's sectarian political system.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.280
We're going to explain that system in a second - but let's get a sense

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.720
of just how tough everyday life is for most Lebanese people.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:16.720
We don't really have access to proper public services.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.920
Like there's no 24/7 electricity, there is no clean, accessible drinking water.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.120
You have piles of garbage all over the country.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.440
Sewage is not treated. It goes straight out into the ocean.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:33.360
So it feels like the state is absent from daily life in Lebanon.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.440
Most people agree that mess is caused by serious mismanagement.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.640
Some say it's because of corruption.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:45.360
But you'll also hear analysts say that Lebanon never really recovered from a long and devastating war.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:59.800
We’re talking about Lebanon’s civil war which started in 1975 and went on for 15 years.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:06.600
Militias from different sects and political groups fought each other for dominance, and also fought among themselves.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:11.160
Then Syria and Israel got involved, and the battles became even more destructive.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:16.360
At the end of the war, Lebanon’s main political groups signed the Taif Agreement

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:19.960
to make sure they all got a slice of political power.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.440
And that’s really the basis for Lebanon’s political system today.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.640
A Maronite Christian gets the presidency, the prime minister has to be Sunni Muslim,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.440
and the speaker of parliament is always a Shia Muslim.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.720
In Parliament, seats are shared 50/50 - between Muslims and Christians.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:41.960
But in reality, there are two big political alliances which include parties

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:46.360
from different sects, and they each have rival foreign powers backing them.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:52.680
March 14 was former Prime Minister Saad Hariri’s bloc, which has the support of Saudi Arabia and the US. 

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:58.520
March 8 is the bloc that includes the Maronite Christian President Michel Aoun’s party and Hezbollah.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.560
It has Syria and Iran’s support.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:06.040
So because of all those overlapping and competing interests, 

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:10.520
many people will tell you that Lebanon’s sectarian political system isn’t really sectarian.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:16.760
What's really happening in Lebanon is that there are political parties that used to be militias.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:24.680
Sects are not fighting in Lebanon. It's really opposing warlords backed by opposing foreign powers.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:29.120
And this is how - many say - corruption has gotten so out of hand.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.120
Many of those powerful political leaders - or the Zuama as they’re called in Lebanon - are said to have focused

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.920
on their own political and financial gains and made themselves very rich.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:47.560
Lebanon has 220 kilometres of coast. 180 kilometres of the coast has been privatized.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:54.360
It's now under the control of either former officials and people who are close to them.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:07:00.240
I'll just give you one example of parking meters in Beirut. The revenues were not going to the state.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:06.320
They were going to a private company controlled owned by people who are close to politicians.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.680
There have been no real signs of change since then.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:15.280
And how the port is allowed to run is seen as a big part of the problem.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.520
In his coverage of the explosion our Beirut correspondent put it this way: 

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:23.920
“It is also not lost on Beirut's residents that this tragedy emanated from the city's port

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:29.200
a public utility known locally as the Cave of Ali Baba and the 40 Thieves.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:35.960
He talks about allegations of bribes — and billions of dollars in tax revenue from the port disappearing.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:41.040
And since the pandemic things have gone from bad to worse.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.160
The government is nearly bankrupt. 

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:48.280
Lebanon already had the world’s third-highest level of debt relative to its GDP.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:53.240
Its currency, the lira, has lost 85% of its value against the dollar.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:08:00.360
And inflation is rising by more than 50% a month. Food has become unaffordable for so many people.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:12.320
Back in January people had hoped a new government would improve things.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:17.320
Their main goal this year was to push through reforms to qualify for international aid.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:23.320
But the politicians haven’t been able to agree and talks with the International Monetary Fund are on hold. 

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:29.480
It's not anger for the sake of anger. It's not an impossibility to have in Lebanon

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.520
competent people to govern and to serve their people.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.120
Let there be accountability. Let's have a transparent investigation.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:43.240
Right now people in Lebanon are asking themselves how in the world the country is ever going to recover.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.760
Who’s going to rebuild Beirut?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:51.240
And where’s the money going to come from to pay for an estimated $15BN worth of damage? 

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.880
How is its health system going to treat thousands of injured people

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.560
and people sick with COVID-19 after at least three hospitals have been destroyed?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.640
And where is a country that’s almost entirely reliant on imports from the sea

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.720
going to get food from when its port is a crater?

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.560
Even before the explosion politicians in Lebanon couldn’t find common ground.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:21.680
So now something and someone’s gotta give to stand any chance of sorting out this mess.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.880
Because you can only push people so far.

